Plinius: "Hardware" in System, the phone's chips and firmware versions.

A row above About opens a page with the components (SoC, graphics, storage, Wi-Fi and
Bluetooth chip, touchscreen, NFC, wireless charging, audio), the firmware that starts before
Linux (preloader, bootloader, Trusted Firmware-A, trusted OSes, hypervisor, power management,
verified boot), the radios (modem, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth) and the Android vendor side, each with
version and build date. The device package collects them at boot as root into
/run/plinius-hardware (plinius-hardware-info); without its collector the row stays hidden.

The page (cc-plinius-hardware.*) lives as a separate file in the package directory and is
copied to panels/system/ in prepare().

